  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The function $\\log |x|$ is not defined at $x=0$, so, $\\mathrm{x}=0$ is a point of discontinuity. Also for $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})$ to be defined, $\\log |\\mathrm{x}| \\neq 0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x} \\neq\\pm 1$\r\n\r\nHence, 0,1,-1 are three points of discontinuity.",
    "image": null
